      en: "The Old Supreme Court Building in Central, built in 1912, is a magnificent neoclassical building with an impressive dome and Ionic columns. It served as the Supreme Court of Hong Kong from 1912 to 1985. During the Japanese occupation, it was used as a headquarters by the Japanese. After the war, it resumed as a court, and since 1985, it houses the Legislative Council meetings. The building is a symbol of the rule of law in Hong Kong and a prime example of colonial architecture. It survived urban development and was declared a monument in 1992. The interiors are richly decorated with marble and woodwork, highlighting its significance.",
